+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository layer
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, createdAt)` that, in one transaction (`BEGIN` … `COMMIT`, `ROLLBACK` on error), updates `orders.discount_cents`/`final_amount_cents`/`coupon_code`, inserts a `coupon_redemptions` row, and increments `coupons.used_count`; verify `npm run build` passes and a focused test shows an error mid-transaction leaves no changes
+
+## 2. Service layer
+
+- [x] 2.1 Add `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, body)` implementing REQ-13 body validation, the order checks, coupon lookup, status/validity/usage/minimum checks in the error-table order, and return the re-read order; verify with tests for `INVALID_REQUEST`, `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`, `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED`, `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, `COUPON_INACTIVE`
+- [x] 2.2 Implement discount computation (`FIXED`, `PERCENT` with `Math.round(amountCents * value / 100)`, `maxDiscountCents` cap, clamp to `amountCents`) and verify with tests for the amount/minimum/validity/usage cases and the FIXED/PERCENT/cap/clamp math
+
+## 3. HTTP layer and wiring
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `routes/orders.ts` and give `OrderService` a `CouponRepository` dependency in `app.ts`; verify `npm run build` passes
+- [x] 3.2 Add endpoint tests asserting HTTP 200 and that the response body equals a subsequent `GET /orders/:id`; verify they pass
+- [x] 3.3 Add tests for code normalization (`" save20 "` matches `SAVE20`) and for the success side effects (coupon `usedCount` +1, one new `coupon_redemptions` row, rejected requests change nothing)
+
+## 4. Verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` and confirm both pass with the existing tests unchanged
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after review requirements are satisfied.
